{number: 24}
{title: Joy to the World! The Lord Is Come}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D] Joy to the world! the [G] Lord is [A] come:
Let [D] earth receive her [A] King;
Let [D] every [D7] heart pre-[G] pare Him room,
And [D] heaven and nature sing,
And [A] heaven and nature sing,
And [D] heaven, and [G] heaven [D] and na-[A] ture [D] sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[D] Joy to the earth! the [G] Savior [A] reigns:
Let [D] men their songs em-[A] ploy;
While [D] fields and [D7] floods, rocks, [G] hills, and plains
Re-[D] peat the sounding joy,
Re-[A] peat the sounding joy,
Re-[D] peat, re-[G] peat, [D] the soun-[A] ding [D] joy.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[D] No more let sins and [G] sorrows [A] grow,
Nor [D] thorns infest the [A] ground;
He [D] comes to [D7] make His [G] blessings flow
Far [D] as the curse is found,
Far [A] as the curse is found,
Far [D] as, far [G] as, [D] the cur-[A] se is [D] found.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[D] He rules the world with [G] truth and [A] grace,
And [D] makes the nations [A] prove
The [D] glories [D7] of His [G] righteousness,
And [D] wonders of His love,
And [A] wonders of His love,
And [D] wonders, [G] wonders, [D] of [A] His [D] love.
{end_of_verse}
